[{:db/id "q-116791/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cb5bcaa4-1b63-5031-b962-452b43860d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1f40063f-6332-5a1f-a75a-57962e741ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "17852096-19ed-5310-9959-9334976df9e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "97c31d5e-7d98-574d-b338-e4fafbddc378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4efda690-b77f-5ce3-9057-144430b4993a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b204b910-62ff-5aea-b3be-59c5dba8548c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116791/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-116791/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-116791/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-116791/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-116791/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-116791/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116791" :question/id #uuid "0383dba8-2813-5055-8721-ce87ccaa233e" :question/math-academy-id "q-116791" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}x+2,\\,y(0)=-1.\n$$\n\nUse the tangent line approximation of $y(x)$ at $x=0$ to approximate $y(0.5).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $y(x)$ at the point $a=0$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(a)+{y}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =y(0)+{y}^{′}(0)(x-0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the initial condition, we know that $y(0)=-1.$ We also know that ${y}^{′}(x)={y}^{2}x+2,$ so\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=(-1)^{2}\\cdot 0+2=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $y(0)$ and ${y}^{′}(0)$ into our expression for $L(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(0)+{y}^{′}(0)(x-0) \\\\  & =-1+(2)(x-0) \\\\  & =2x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can approximate $y(0.5)$ using $L(0.5).$ We get\n\n$$\ny(0.5)≈L(0.5)=2(0.5)-1=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "982052d0-32dc-557a-b501-cfb011787f22"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "22f2b002-4096-50e2-bc69-64a3b85aab8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4c7284bf-bb70-5072-98e4-8d4eb8658a8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection/451e012537131dbb0d5b5d7046e0380b171d9769f5644e4647cfb7fb52590452" :answer/id #uuid "4c5b5dc7-7f5d-5d63-91d6-6ddf9d027039" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" :answer/id #uuid "5180c806-0ece-5431-a8bc-92c83da4433f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection/e1a79fe21dbd63050cc5b8abf7bbfe646e6735d60cb33653e6f487991ef831d5" :answer/id #uuid "c426f1a4-5630-595c-87fe-011a6ad7bf52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "780b8158-5fab-5c3e-b817-97970fbe5874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83382/selection/451e012537131dbb0d5b5d7046e0380b171d9769f5644e4647cfb7fb52590452" :answer-field/choices ["q-83382/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-83382/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-83382/selection/451e012537131dbb0d5b5d7046e0380b171d9769f5644e4647cfb7fb52590452" "q-83382/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" "q-83382/selection/e1a79fe21dbd63050cc5b8abf7bbfe646e6735d60cb33653e6f487991ef831d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83382" :question/id #uuid "0c0185af-134b-51d7-bfef-56a8c9ab82dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-83382" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,y(3)=e.\n$$\n\nUse the tangent line approximation of $y(x)$ at $x=3$ to approximate $y(4).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $y(x)$ at the point $a=3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(a)+{y}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the initial condition, we know that $y(3)=e.$ We also know that ${y}^{′}(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,$ so\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(3)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $y(3)$ and ${y}^{′}(3)$ into our expression for $L(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(3)+{y}^{′}(3)(x-3) \\\\  & =e+(3)(x-3) \\\\  & =3x+e-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can approximate $y(4)$ using $L(4).$ We get\n\n$$\ny(4)≈L(4)=3(4)+e-9=e+3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83382/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "982052d0-32dc-557a-b501-cfb011787f22"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83382"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-53846"] :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y(1)=2.\n$$\n\nUse the tangent line approximation of $y(x)$ at $x=1$ to approximate $y(1.5).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $y(x)$ at the point $a=1$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(a)+{y}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =y(1)+{y}^{′}(1)(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the initial condition, we know that $y(1)=2.$ We also know that ${y}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x},$ so\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $y(1)$ and ${y}^{′}(1)$ into our expression for $L(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =y(1)+{y}^{′}(1)(x-1) \\\\  & =2+(1)(x-1) \\\\  & =x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can approximate $y(1.5)$ using $L(1.5).$ We get\n\n$$\ny(1.5)≈L(1.5)=1.5+1=2.5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86900"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3x-4y,\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $Δy$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $$ | $$ | $\\,?\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=2,$ we fill $y=2$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =3x-4y \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-353294/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "82abea2e-2698-5042-85b3-43ba773a0904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353294/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "fa84a6ba-ce07-53cb-8bdd-8e9057103d16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353294/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2938f41-83b9-552b-a539-5586d3dcefb8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353294/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-353294/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-353294/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353294" :question/id #uuid "9a44b2ed-9e07-52d2-88b9-0807d282c038" :question/math-academy-id "q-353294" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+2y,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Fill in the empty box in the column for $Δy$ in the table below using this method. Do not round the answer.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=1,$ we fill $y=1$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+2y \\\\  & =1+2(1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353294/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e731217-ca61-5295-aeb5-0c3febd250d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347894/field-1/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" :answer/id #uuid "1ea76f7e-c100-5cd7-8dcb-77d89d711637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347894/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5622b436-8933-5c60-9540-a9eca6a5015e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347894/field-1/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" :answer-field/choices ["q-347894/field-1/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347894" :question/id #uuid "212e7734-0cbb-592e-ba04-76f0045ec8bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-347894" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-1,\\,y(-1)=2\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method with step size $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Fill in the empty box in the column for $Δy$ in the table below using this method. Do not round the answer.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $$ | $$ | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(-1)=2,$ we fill $y=2$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x{y}^{2}-1 \\\\  & =(-1)(2)^{2}-1 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =-5(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $-\\frac{5}{4}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347894/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e731217-ca61-5295-aeb5-0c3febd250d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "c118e557-66e7-5c77-b2e9-c6f5e4f9fc37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "80c77bf1-f889-54cf-abb6-a44e6a56ea98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "11f1a4ac-0149-53b7-9cc7-1d372e0d69c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "8aa6b35b-582f-5000-b382-16b238ff2dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "25185c39-076a-5a9f-82f5-267a439e9653" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6ee4c6-aa0c-5764-9ae8-375c27cd1345" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116878/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-116878/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-116878/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-116878/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-116878/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" "q-116878/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116878" :question/id #uuid "56338bc4-f0b6-5400-8fc1-d56b70cb9bd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-116878" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y-7x,\\,y(1)=3\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $Δy$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{6}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $$ | $$ | $\\,?\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=3,$ we fill $y=3$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2y-7x \\\\  & =2(3)-7(1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{6}$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-116878/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e731217-ca61-5295-aeb5-0c3febd250d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353298/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "495aa644-b3b9-5812-b635-aa47c8c1cc43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353298/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fe7b96c-88cf-5338-a62d-14d87cc5a9f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353298/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-353298/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353298" :question/id #uuid "3e7d6a4e-83e6-5b6d-8420-c1aa32525b83" :question/math-academy-id "q-353298" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y-2x,\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method with step size $Δx=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Fill in the empty box in the column for $Δy$ in the table below using this method. Do not round the answer.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(0)=-2,$ we fill $y=-2$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y-2x \\\\  & =-2-2(0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $-3$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-353298/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e731217-ca61-5295-aeb5-0c3febd250d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353298"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0d70ccee-a7c3-55f1-bf21-d871bff2060e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "46410034-8440-5fcb-a319-fae3c6cd57ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "62577b90-31b9-5228-b770-a6013846a0d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "a91dd5c7-7798-51fe-8782-62452fb152b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "3bd798e4-dae1-5f8b-9c1b-b6ed858f72be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aef02c17-9352-5e12-beca-5d1d85015aec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116886/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-116886/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-116886/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-116886/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-116886/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-116886/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116886" :question/id #uuid "8fcc07d8-65cb-5436-81ed-f2735989e3bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-116886" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2xy,\\,y(-1)=3\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the cell indicated in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\,?\\,$ | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(-1)=3,$ we fill $y=3$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2xy \\\\  & =2(-1)(3) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =3+(-3) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(-\\frac{1}{2})≈0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116886/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0eb0c7f2-a559-5324-8778-ca5cab083864"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353307/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d67ca3f0-5dcd-50a1-8ee0-20e5f8ffa181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353307/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a7efb56c-1d2f-5d4c-ab60-1e8c25f48122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353307/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "425a043a-7742-55da-a662-9c7a9cebbb29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353307/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-353307/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-353307/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353307" :question/id #uuid "a39add82-ab88-59e9-8e84-cd25649c9370" :question/math-academy-id "q-353307" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\sqrt{3x+4}+y,\\,y(4)=-1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method with step size $Δx=1.$ Fill in the empty box in the table below using this method. Do not round the answer.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n| $5$ | {{field-1}} | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(4)=-1,$ we fill $y=-1$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt{3x+4}+y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3(4)+4}+(-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16}-1 \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =3(1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =-1+3 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(5)≈2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353307/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0eb0c7f2-a559-5324-8778-ca5cab083864"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353325/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "8081d013-8366-5453-852a-caae174c94e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353325/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d685e99-d281-5d9e-959c-31ba547aef9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353325/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer-field/choices ["q-353325/field-1/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353325" :question/id #uuid "4eddbf6a-7384-5c89-ae2f-33e9958b3093" :question/math-academy-id "q-353325" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x(2y-1),\\,y(\\frac{1}{2})=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with one step to approximate $y(1).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$y(1)≈$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of \n\n$$\nΔx=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we add the initial condition data:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x(2y-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈\\frac{5}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-353325/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0eb0c7f2-a559-5324-8778-ca5cab083864"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353325"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-86975"] :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=5x+6y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with one step to approximate $y(1).$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=1,$ we will use a step size of \n\n$$\nΔx=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we add the initial condition data:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5x+6y \\\\  & =5\\cdot (0)+6\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(6)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $6$ | $6$ |\n| $1$ | $7$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(1)≈7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "383d67ef-b0f9-5782-bea5-a0da5463f3bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "802588af-cf3b-5a8e-a543-9e32e92a4801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c4aa0382-4fe1-580b-855f-82f636f47bcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "f1763dcc-5c13-58c7-811c-c1bc53bd040c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "caf93316-9376-55b4-8226-6969dc25239e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c5da0a-013d-5da6-8eaa-e5f83cbd6d81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116773/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-116773/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-116773/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-116773/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-116773/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-116773/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116773" :question/id #uuid "d3a86cf7-ac7c-5cf3-be46-a948a6ac4cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-116773" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2xy,\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the cell indicated in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ |  | $$ | $$ |\n| $2$ | $\\,?\\,$ | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, because the initial condition is $y(1)=1,$ we fill $y=1$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2xy \\\\  & =2\\cdot (1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $2$ | $3$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116773/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0eb0c7f2-a559-5324-8778-ca5cab083864"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
